# Aira Environment Variables
#
# For production: store all secrets in AWS Secrets Manager (aria/secrets).
# For CI/CD: use GitHub Actions encrypted secrets (Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions).
# For local dev: copy this file to .env and fill in values.
#                .env is gitignored — never commit real secrets.

# ── AWS Secrets Manager ────────────────────────────────────────────
# When these are set, config.ts loads secrets from AWS Secrets Manager first,
# falling back to the env vars below for local development.
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# AWS_SECRET_ID=aira/secrets

# ── Drata API ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DRATA_API_KEY=sk_your_drata_api_key_here
DRATA_BASE_URL=https://public-api.drata.com/public/v2

# ── Google Gemini (Vertex AI) ──────────────────────────────────────
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# ── GCP Evidence Collection (ISO 27001 A.8) ─────────────────────────
# GCP_PROJECT_ID=your-gcp-project-id
# GCP_ORGANIZATION_ID=your-gcp-org-id
# GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY={"type":"service_account","project_id":"...","private_key_id":"...","private_key":"..."}
# For production, store GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY in AWS Secrets Manager
# at aira/secrets/gcp-evidence-collector instead.

# ── OpenRouter (AI Fallback) ────────────────────────────────────────
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-your_openrouter_api_key_here

# ── Compliance role mailbox (RBR-759 / RBR-766) ─────────────────────
# Used by scripts/compliance_mailbox.py for vendor outreach (ISO 27001 RFQs,
# pen-test vendors, insurers, customer security questionnaires).
#
# NEVER put the mailbox password here as a literal. It is resolved, in order:
#   1. COMPLIANCE_MAILBOX_PASSWORD      — injected by Paperclip from a company
#                                         secret via secret_ref (production)
#   2. COMPLIANCE_MAILBOX_PASSWORD_CMD  — command that prints it (keychain/pass)
#   3. AWS Secrets Manager aira/secrets -> COMPLIANCE_MAILBOX_PASSWORD
# See docs/compliance-role-mailbox-rbr759.md.
#
# CEO decision on RBR-398 (comment 4c573d62): dispatch the CB RFQs from
# ben.hamilton@aira.io — a Workspace user on the certified domain, so it needs
# no Workspace admin work. security@aira.io conversion stays on RBR-759 as the
# permanent home and is off the critical path.
#
# NOTE (RBR-775): "login-capable" is NOT yet proven. Google returns
# 'Invalid credentials' both for a real mailbox and for an address that does
# not exist, so the earlier IMAP probe was indeterminate. Only a passing
# `selftest` proves it. dispatch_rfqs_rbr766.sh gates on that and fails closed.
#
# To supply the credential:  ./scripts/store_compliance_mailbox_password.sh
COMPLIANCE_MAILBOX_ADDRESS=ben.hamilton@aira.io
COMPLIANCE_MAILBOX_PROFILE=google
COMPLIANCE_MAILBOX_DISPLAY_NAME=Ben Hamilton, CISO — Aira (Rambur Inc.)
# COMPLIANCE_MAILBOX_PASSWORD_CMD=security find-generic-password -s aira-compliance-mailbox -a ben.hamilton@aira.io -w

# ── Data ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DATA_DIR=./data